# Stack conventions

Sunnex Clothing is a single Next.js App Router app (TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Prisma, PostgreSQL, Auth.js).

- Colocate routes under `app/`. Put shared UI in `components/`, domain helpers in `lib/`, schema in `prisma/`.
- Use Server Components by default. Add `"use client"` only for interactivity.
- Mutations go through Server Actions or route handlers with Zod validation and server-side role checks.
- Keep Prisma in server-only modules. Never import the database client into Client Components.
- Names: `client` for customers of the house, not generic `user`, except for the auth `User` model.
- Match existing folder patterns once the app is scaffolded. Do not add a separate API framework.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — db in the browser
"use client";
import { prisma } from "@/lib/db";

// ✅ GOOD — server action
"use server";
export async function saveClient(input: unknown) {
  const data = clientSchema.parse(input);
  await requireStaff();
  return prisma.client.create({ data });
}
```
